Holy Week procession is a public ritual march of clergy and penitents which takes place during Holy week in Christian Countries especially those with a Catholic culture.
Various images of the saints, especially the Virgin Mary, and most importantly the image of the crucified Christ are carried aloft by foot on shoulder-borne pasos (or on wheeled carrozas in the Philippines) as an act of penance; acts of mortifocation are carried out; traditional Christian hymns  and chants are sung (except during the silent processions of Good Friday).
@RexieAndJasTravels

